# Ultron — one line ending policy, applied once.
#
# The tree grew both endings: 39 modules were CRLF, the documents were LF, and a
# patch tool had to ask each file which it was. This file is the answer, and the
# commit that added it also renormalised every stored blob, so the repository and
# the working tree now agree and never have to guess again.
#
#   * source and documents: LF, stored and checked out;
#   * the Windows launchers: CRLF, because cmd.exe and PowerShell read them
#     (tests/test_launchers.py asserts this, byte by byte);
#   * binaries: marked, so no diff tries to read them as text.
#
# To change the policy later, change this file and run `git add --renormalize .`
# in ONE commit, then say so in log.txt. Never let a line ending change ride
# along inside a feature commit.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf

*.bat   text eol=crlf
*.cmd   text eol=crlf
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
*.gif  binary
*.webm binary
*.mp4 binary
*.zip  binary
*.so   binary
*.dll  binary
